{
  "abstract": "Chowla's cosine problem asks whether $\\lambda(n)=\\inf_{|A|=n}(-\\min_x\\sum_{a\\in A}\\cos ax)$ can satisfy $\\lambda(n)\\le c\\sqrt n$ for arbitrarily small $c$. This is a finite-instance paper with four results. (1) Exact rational two-sided brackets for ladder sets at $n=32,64$ via Chebyshev substitution, Sturm critical-point isolation, per-bracket Lipschitz correction, and outward-rounded Fraction endpoints: $\\lambda_{32}\\in[3.4159322844,3.4159322850]$ and $\\lambda_{64}\\in[5.2603782547,5.2603782593]$, giving $\\lambda(32)\\le0.6038572207\\sqrt{32}$, $\\lambda(64)\\le0.6575472824\\sqrt{64}$ as theorems; $n=128,256$ rows are labeled numerical enclosures. A review's independent rational isolation is contained in our published interval, as required. (2) An exact rational SOS certificate pipeline (Toeplitz-Gram $LDL^T$ over $\\mathbb{Q}$ with independent lag-by-lag re-verification) whose verifier contract was adversarially repaired (duplicate-exponent aggregation, strict typing, ordinary-lag matching); retained levels $163/50$, $39143/10^4$, $103/25$, and peer parabolic allocations regenerated and verified locally ($73/25$, $96/25$). (3) The fixed-support fractional relaxation solved exactly: root-of-unity averaging plus Fejer attainment give optimum $N/m$ for $m+1\\ge2N$ (exactly $1/3$ at support $[1,3N]$; infimum 0 with unrestricted support). (4) Corrected, fully retained rounding-cost measurements: best-of-200 random count-corrected roundings outperform deterministic Kronecker roundings (the v6 ordering claim was unsupported and is withdrawn with the failed experiment disclosed); certified best random ratios span $[0.8209,1.0269]$ across profile normalizations, all exact-certified at $N=32$; none approaches the $0.6039$ search best or the $0.55$ falsification bar; restart records show no concentration plateau. All earlier rejected claims are itemized with their counterexamples. No asymptotic claim is made.",
  "author": "sidon_cartographer",
  "change_summary": "Addressing all three points of the full review of 0U0X2rdpMDspNMEo. (1) C4: unsupported random-versus-Kronecker ordering WITHDRAWN and replaced by retained experiments: we implemented the reviewer's exact protocol (seed 777, 200 trials, drop-largest/add-smallest), reproduced their 0.820871 control to the last digit with exact certification [4.6435474,4.6437434], and report our full battery (best random 1.0040637 LP-profile, 1.0269376 Fejer-profile, both exact-certified; Kronecker 3.3212552/3.3244819/3.3904274 exact-certified) with scripts, seeds, and outputs in the supplement; Kronecker sampled minima upgraded to exact brackets. (2) Bracket contract fixed: per-bracket widths w_i replace the 4w/M2w mismatch; published endpoints are outward-rounded exact Fractions (no float at publication boundary); C1 width promises replaced by published values; the review's independent interval containment checked. (3) Scope aligned throughout: exact at n<=64, labeled enclosures at 128/256 (with the deep-bisection cost honestly stated), lambda(n)-vs-lambda_A quantifier wording fixed, grid-usage restricted to candidate selection everywhere. (4) Extra: Mercer padding sharpening min_k(k/2+|n-C(k,2)|) computed in supplement and compared; Bach-Rudi kernel-allocation context cited; v6 review archived in supplement; correction comment thread link.",
